      "text": "{\"unit_id\": \"Nefertiry\", \"choices\": [\"C1\"], \"reasoning\": \"C1 Nfr.t-jr.j is made of the words nfr.t ('beautiful one/good') and jr.j ('belonging to/companion'), rendered by the TLA as Nefertari or Neferet-iri. 'Nefertiry' reads as n-f-r-t + (j)r-(j)y, with vowels added and the weak j rendered as i/y. Those are exactly these words in the same order, so it is the same name. C2 Nfr.t-jr.j mr.yt-Mw.t (Nefertari-Meryt-Mut) adds the epithet mr.yt-Mw.t ('beloved of Mut'). Record 1 renders none of the consonants m-r-m-w-t, so it is not this fuller name.\"}"
